---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { TEMPLATES } from '../../scripts/anagrammer/templates.js';

const repoUrl = 'https://github.com/kristenbestavros/anagrammer';
---

<Base
  title="Anagrammer"
  description="A hybrid Markov and phonotactics engine that rearranges any phrase into plausible names. Ported to run in the browser."
>
  <article class="section">
    <header class="page-head">
      <p class="label">2026 · personal · Python + browser port</p>
      <div>
        <h1 class="page-title">Anagrammer</h1>
        <p class="lede head-lede">
          When writing, I sometimes enjoy giving my characters names that are 
          anagrams of some meaningful word or phrase. Doing this by hand is tedious,
          so I made this tool to help me out. Given any input text, it rearranges every letter 
          into fictional character names that sound plausible and pronounceable.
        </p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="demo" aria-labelledby="demo-heading">
      <h3 id="demo-heading" class="visually-hidden">Try it</h3>

      <div class="demo-controls">
        <div class="field field-wide">
          <label class="label" for="ana-input">Phrase</label>
          <input
            id="ana-input"
            type="text"
            value="necessary evil"
            autocomplete="off"
            spellcheck="false"
            maxlength="40"
          />
        </div>

        <div class="field">
          <label class="label" for="ana-dataset">Names</label>
          <select id="ana-dataset">
            <option value="both">All</option>
            <option value="female">Feminine</option>
            <option value="male">Masculine</option>
          </select>
        </div>

        <div class="field">
          <label class="label" for="ana-template">Format</label>
          <select id="ana-template">
            <option value="">Auto</option>
            {TEMPLATES.map((t) => <option value={t.label}>{t.label}</option>)}
          </select>
        </div>

        <div class="field">
          <label class="label" for="ana-temp">Sampling</label>
          <select id="ana-temp">
            <option value="ramp">Default ramp</option>
            <option value="1.0">Conservative</option>
            <option value="1.6">Balanced</option>
            <option value="2.6">Diverse</option>
          </select>
        </div>

        <div class="field">
          <label class="label" for="ana-count">Results</label>
          <select id="ana-count">
            <option value="5">5</option>
            <option value="10" selected>10</option>
            <option value="15">15</option>
          </select>
        </div>

        <button id="ana-go" type="button" disabled>Loading model</button>
      </div>

      <div class="demo-extra">
        <label class="check">
          <input id="ana-allow-words" type="checkbox" />
          <span>Allow real English words as names</span>
        </label>
        <label class="check seed">
          <span class="label">Seed</span>
          <input id="ana-seed" type="text" inputmode="numeric" placeholder="random" />
        </label>
      </div>

      <div id="ana-out" class="demo-out" role="status" aria-live="polite">
        <p class="out-msg">Fetching the trained model…</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="body">
      <h2 class="section-heading">How it works</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          The algorithm combines multiple generation tactics at different steps. A trigram
          character model trained on about 106,000 real names decides what letter sequences
          are the most name-like; a set of phonotactic rules ensure the names are pronounceable; and a
          composite scoring function ranks hundreds of candidates and returns the best ones.
        </p>
        <p>
          Generating a plausible name using a machine learning model based on real names
          is not difficult, and there are many such generators available online. Making a name-like anagram
          is more complicated, since the model can never simply take the most
          likely next character; it can only choose from letters that haven't been used yet.
        </p>

        <h3>The pipeline</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Template selection.</strong> Ten name structures, from a
            bare mononym to <em>First Middle Middle Last-Last</em>. Only the ones
            whose length bounds fit your letter count are eligible, and
            hyphenated surnames unlock at sixteen letters.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Guided construction.</strong> Each segment is built one
            character at a time, sampling from the Markov distribution over
            letters still available, with temperature controlling how closely it
            follows the model. 
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Phonotactic lookahead.</strong> Candidate letters that would
            walk the segment into a dead end are filtered before they're
            sampled — invalid onset clusters, more than three consonants in a
            row, vowel pairs English doesn't use, a segment about to end with no
            vowel in it at all.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Letter distribution.</strong> Any letters left stranded at
            the end are inserted back into existing segments at whichever
            position costs the least likelihood.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Composite scoring.</strong> Candidates are ranked on Markov
            likelihood per character, length balance across segments, distance
            from a natural ~40% vowel ratio, starting-letter variety, repeated
            bigrams, and how cleanly the end of one segment runs into the start
            of the next.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Filtering and diverse selection.</strong> Segments matching
            any of ~8,000 common English words are rejected. Final picks are made
            greedily with a penalty for reusing segments so that the list doesn't get saturated with ten
            variations on one letter sequence.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h3>What this browser version leaves out</h3>
        <p>
          The full tool adds two refinement passes after construction:
          hill-climbing that swaps individual letters between segments, then a
          second pass that swaps whole syllables to find improvements
          single-letter moves can't reach. Those are the most intricate part of
          the codebase and the least visible on a single query, so they aren't
          ported here.
        </p>
        <p>
          Everything else is the same algorithm working from the same trained
          model, and the scoring function agrees with the Python to six decimal
          places. The command-line version also supports locking in a specific
          first or last name, reproducible seeding, and verbose diagnostics.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a class="arrow-link" href={repoUrl}>Source on GitHub</a>
        </p>

        <h3>Notes</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>
            Everything runs in your browser. The model is a static file; nothing
            you type is sent anywhere.
          </li>
          <li>
            Name data comes from Kate Monk's Onomastikon (© 1997 Kate Monk),
            covering naming traditions worldwide.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>

  <style>
    .head-lede {
      margin-top: 1rem;
    }

    .body {
      margin-top: 3.4rem;
    }

    .mono {
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      font-size: 0.85em;
    }

    .demo {
      margin-top: 2.8rem;
      background: var(--raised);
      border: 1px solid var(--rule);
      padding: 1.6rem;
    }

    .demo-controls {
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: 1rem 1.3rem;
      align-items: flex-end;
    }

    .field {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 0.35rem;
      min-width: 7rem;
    }

    .field-wide {
      flex: 1 1 14rem;
    }

    .demo input[type='text'],
    .demo select {
      font-family: var(--font-body);
      font-size: 0.95rem;
      color: var(--ink);
      background: var(--paper);
      border: 1px solid var(--rule);
      border-radius: 2px;
      padding: 0.5rem 0.6rem;
      width: 100%;
    }

    .demo button {
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      font-size: 0.74rem;
      letter-spacing: 0.1em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: var(--paper);
      background: var(--ink);
      border: 1px solid var(--ink);
      border-radius: 2px;
      padding: 0.62rem 1.1rem;
      cursor: pointer;
      transition: background 0.15s ease;
    }

    .demo button:hover:not(:disabled) {
      background: var(--accent);
      border-color: var(--accent);
    }

    .demo button:disabled {
      background: var(--muted);
      border-color: var(--muted);
      cursor: default;
    }

    .demo-extra {
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: 0.6rem 1.6rem;
      align-items: center;
      margin-top: 1.1rem;
    }

    .check {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 0.5rem;
      font-size: 0.85rem;
      color: var(--muted);
      cursor: pointer;
    }

    .check input[type='checkbox'] {
      accent-color: var(--accent);
    }

    .seed input {
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      font-size: 0.8rem;
      width: 7rem;
      background: var(--paper);
      border: 1px solid var(--rule);
      border-radius: 2px;
      padding: 0.3rem 0.45rem;
      color: var(--ink);
    }

    .demo-out {
      margin-top: 1.6rem;
      padding-top: 1.4rem;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
      min-height: 8rem;
    }

    .demo-out :global(.out-msg) {
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      font-size: 0.78rem;
      letter-spacing: 0.04em;
      color: var(--muted);
      margin: 0;
      max-width: none;
    }

    .demo-out :global(.out-head) {
      justify-content: space-between;
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      font-size: 0.68rem;
      letter-spacing: 0.06em;
      color: var(--muted);
      margin: 0 0 1rem;
      max-width: none;
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: 0.3rem 1.2rem;
    }

    .demo-out :global(.results) {
      list-style: none;
      margin: 0;
      padding: 0;
    }

    .demo-out :global(.results li) {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: 0.2rem 0.9rem;
      align-items: baseline;
      padding: 0.62rem 0;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
    }

    .results li:last-child {
      border-bottom: 0;
    }

    .demo-out :global(.rank) {
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      font-size: 0.7rem;
      color: var(--muted);
    }

    .demo-out :global(.name) {
      font-family: var(--font-display);
      font-size: 1.32rem;
      line-height: 1.25;
    }

    .meta {
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      font-size: 0.66rem;
      letter-spacing: 0.04em;
      color: var(--muted);
      text-align: right;
      white-space: nowrap;
    }

    .meta .ok {
      color: var(--accent);
    }

    .tmpl {
      grid-column: 2;
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      font-size: 0.64rem;
      letter-spacing: 0.05em;
      color: var(--muted);
    }

      @media (max-width: 34rem) {
      .demo-out :global(.results li) {
        grid-template-columns: 1.4rem minmax(0, 1fr);
      }
    }
  </style>

  <script>
    import { randomSeed } from '../../scripts/anagrammer/rng.js';

    const $ = (id) => document.getElementById(id);
    const out = $('ana-out');
    const button = $('ana-go');
    const seedField = $('ana-seed');

    const worker = new Worker(
      new URL('../../scripts/anagrammer/worker.js', import.meta.url),
      { type: 'module' }
    );

    let busy = false;

    function message(text) {
      out.innerHTML = `<p class="out-msg">${text}</p>`;
    }

    function escapeHtml(s) {
      return s.replace(/[&<>"]/g, (c) =>
        ({ '&': '&amp;', '<': '&lt;', '>': '&gt;', '"': '&quot;' })[c]
      );
    }

    worker.postMessage({
      type: 'init',
      url: new URL('/data/anagram-data.json', location.origin).href,
    });

    worker.onmessage = (event) => {
      const msg = event.data;

      if (msg.type === 'ready') {
        button.disabled = false;
        button.textContent = 'Generate names';
        run();
        return;
      }

      if (msg.type === 'failed') {
        busy = false;
        button.disabled = false;
        button.textContent = 'Generate names';
        message(`Something went wrong: ${escapeHtml(msg.message)}`);
        return;
      }

      if (msg.type === 'results') {
        busy = false;
        button.disabled = false;
        button.textContent = 'Generate names';

        if (msg.error === 'too-short') {
          message('Needs at least three letters.');
          return;
        }
        if (msg.error === 'too-long') {
          message(
            `${msg.letters.length} letters is more than the longest name format can hold. Try 35 or fewer.`
          );
          return;
        }
        if (msg.error === 'template-unfit') {
          const [lo, hi] = msg.templateRange;
          message(
            `That format takes ${lo}–${hi} letters and you gave it ${msg.letters.length}. Try Auto, or a different format.`
          );
          return;
        }
        if (!msg.results.length) {
          message(
            'No arrangement found. These letters are awkward — try a different format, more conservative sampling, or a phrase with more vowels.'
          );
          return;
        }

        // To show diagnostics again, add back inside the <li>:
        //   <span class="meta">${r.score.toFixed(1)} · ${r.exact ? 'exact' : 'mismatch'}</span>
        //   <span class="tmpl">${escapeHtml(r.template)}</span>
        // and restore the third grid column on .results li.
        const rows = msg.results
          .map(
            (r) => `
            <li>
              <span class="name">${escapeHtml(r.name)}</span>
            </li>`
          )
          .join('');

        out.innerHTML =
          `<p class="out-head"><span>${msg.letters.length} letters: ${escapeHtml(
            msg.letters.split('').sort().join('')
          )}</span><span>seed ${msg.seed}</span></p>` +
          `<ul class="results">${rows}</ul>`;
      }
    };

    function run() {
      if (busy) return;
      busy = true;
      button.disabled = true;
      button.textContent = 'Working';
      message('Searching for arrangements…');

      const tempChoice = $('ana-temp').value;
      const temps =
        tempChoice === 'ramp'
          ? {}
          : { tempMin: parseFloat(tempChoice), tempMax: parseFloat(tempChoice) };

      const typedSeed = seedField.value.trim();
      const seed = /^\d+$/.test(typedSeed) ? parseInt(typedSeed, 10) : randomSeed();

      worker.postMessage({
        type: 'generate',
        phrase: $('ana-input').value,
        options: {
          dataset: $('ana-dataset').value,
          nResults: parseInt($('ana-count').value, 10),
          templateLabel: $('ana-template').value || null,
          allowWords: $('ana-allow-words').checked,
          seed,
          ...temps,
        },
      });
    }

    button.addEventListener('click', run);
    $('ana-input').addEventListener('keydown', (e) => {
      if (e.key === 'Enter') run();
    });
  </script>
</Base>
